cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the paper once it is published."
type: software
title: "Node-based tomato FSPM with dual-clock phenology and rule-based leaf pruning"
abstract: "A node-based functional-structural tomato model for greenhouse decision support. Nodes keep their identity, so leaf-pruning rules that read the simulated crop state remove particular leaves on a weekly work schedule. Thermal time and fruit load drive leaf and truss appearance, the source-sink ratio modulates progress from anthesis to fruit set, and fruit temperature drives ripening. Light, photosynthesis, respiration and transpiration are computed hourly for each leaf with a directional Beer's law model of hedgerow canopies. The repository holds the model, the scripts for calibration, evaluation, scenarios and figures, and the calibrated parameter sets."
